        "evidence": "Lean (sibling) `atomicMassGBNF` is a `def` (m_e·ρ_K· | tr_M(NF_GS β) | ): the claimed formula is the definition, nothing asserted. With ρ_K a free positive scalar the statement is contentless: for any mass m and any braid with tr ≠ 0, ρ_K := m/(m_e | tr | ) works. tr_M(NF_GS(B)) = tr_M(B) holds trivially, since the normal form is the same element of H_n. The Lean docstring itself cites a 22–31 % empirical gap for ρ_K"
