        "severity": "major",
        "evidence": "[full review 2026-11-21; scope note rewritten 2026-11-19, 48f446490cc] The Lean is unchanged: atomicMassGBNF is a def equal to the formula, so nothing is asserted, and rho_K is still a free positive scalar. The 2026-11-15 scope note said honestly that the relation 'fixes nothing: any mass is reproduced by choosing rho_K', and that the definition of rho_K is open. The new note replaces this with a claim that the relation 'acquires predictive content' once rho_K is specified through the graded expansion prop:rho-k-graded-expansion (mass-theory/rho-k-graded-expansion.md). That block does not support the claim. (1) It is downstream of this one: it is obtained 'by multiplying the GB-NF identity through', so using it to give this identity content is circular. (2) Its own scope note says only the leading piece is proved, and that piece puts the nucleon and electron masses in by mass additivity. The single-generator piece has a prefactor 'chosen against the mass table', which is a fit under the no-fitting ruling, and the pair-generator piece is open. So rho_K is still not specified independently of m(K), and the old wording was the accurate one. Also the reference is a raw \\ref{prop:rho-k-graded-expansion} rather than a link, and the block is not in uses[]."
      }
